      "text": "Step 1: Factor out the greatest common factor (GCF).\nTo factor out the GCF, we need to find the largest factor that divides evenly into both terms. In this case, the GCF is 3x, since it divides into both 9x^2 and 3x evenly.\n\nStep 2: Write the expression as a product of the GCF and the remaining terms.\n9x^2 can be written as (3x)(3x), and 3x can be written as (3x)(1), since there are no additional factors that will come under the GCF. So, the expression becomes:\n\n(3x)(3x) + (3x)(1)\n\nStep 3: Simplify the expression by recognizing that the GCF can be taken outside of the parentheses.\nThe GCF, which was factored out, is 3x. So, the expression becomes:\n\n(3x)(3x + 1)\n\nFinal answer: The expression 9x^2 + 3x can be completely factored as 3x(3x + 1).",
